---
// Screenshot on the left, the "why" story on the right. Asymmetric, so it doesn't use <Section>.
---

<section class="bg-surface-2 py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl items-center gap-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_1fr] lg:gap-16">
    <img
      src="/screenshot.png"
      width="948"
      height="612"
      loading="lazy"
      class="w-full rounded-xl shadow-[0_24px_64px_-12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] ring-1 ring-black/5"
      alt="The osc window: a sidebar with Documents, Movies, Series and Settings, and a Documents list showing the folders college, docs and notes with their size, file count and date added."
    />
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Why osc exists.</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Storage and RAM kept getting more expensive, and a real NAS was never in the budget.{" "}
        <span class="font-semibold text-link">osc</span> is how I moved my own files off my drive: it treats a private
        Telegram group as storage, and handles the part Telegram doesn't, fast local browsing, low-latency streaming
        with seeking, and a cache that keeps recent files instant.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">Built for my own files first. Sharing it in case it solves the same problem for you.</p>

      <p class="mt-8 flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-8 shrink-0 fill-[#26A5E4]" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M11.944 0A12 12 0 0 0 0 12a12 12 0 0 0 12 12 12 12 0 0 0 12-12A12 12 0 0 0 12 0a12 12 0 0 0-.056 0zm4.962 7.224c.1-.002.321.023.465.14a.506.506 0 0 1 .171.325c.016.093.036.306.02.472-.18 1.898-.962 6.502-1.36 8.627-.168.9-.499 1.201-.82 1.23-.696.065-1.225-.46-1.9-.902-1.056-.693-1.653-1.124-2.678-1.8-1.185-.78-.417-1.21.258-1.91.177-.184 3.247-2.977 3.307-3.23.007-.032.014-.15-.056-.212s-.174-.041-.249-.024c-.106.024-1.793 1.14-5.061 3.345-.48.33-.913.49-1.302.48-.428-.008-1.252-.241-1.865-.44-.752-.245-1.349-.374-1.297-.789.027-.216.325-.437.893-.663 3.498-1.524 5.83-2.529 6.998-3.014 3.332-1.386 4.025-1.627 4.476-1.635z" />
        </svg>
        CREDITS to Telegram's infinite storage BANZAI !!
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
